<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nepal: How are the hundreds of victims from the floods being identified?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c95efce51cff10397f982764ada49c3424cd0692ef48dc82be0aeb89c383c71c</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:54:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:52:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-how-are-the-hundreds-of-victims-from-the-floods-being-identified--61d3ca55ccc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-how-are-the-hundreds-of-victims-from-the-floods-being-identified" /><summary type="html">#Nepal faces a major challenge: identifying the remains that have been found after the #flood that tore through part of the country on August 26, some of which are in an advanced state of decomposition. For #health reasons, the unidentified bodies have begun to be buried. Before each #burial, #DNA samples are taken and an identification number is assigned to each set of remains. Relatives of those reported missing can visit DNA collection centres to provide a sample. Their genetic profile can then be compared with that of the bodies found, in the hope of identifying them. FRANCE 24’s correspondents visited one such centre, set up within the #police #hospital in #Kathmandu.</summary></entry><entry><title>After Nepal’s devastating floods, DNA tests help identify victims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7107831cc208a6bcdb9cc9d5c14b1a2b8795ffefad6e52cbf96d9d0b783a4c48</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:06:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-struggles-to-identify-the-remains-found-in-floods--a15ae8cf314d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-struggles-to-identify-the-remains-found-in-floods" /><summary type="html">The recent flash floods in Nepal have left authorities facing a major challenge: identifying the remains that have been recovered, some of which are in an advanced state of decomposition. For health reasons, unidentified bodies have begun to be buried. Before each burial, DNA samples are taken, while relatives of people reported missing can visit DNA collection centres to provide samples of their own. Their genetic profiles can then be compared with those of the recovered remains, in the hope of identifying them. FRANCE 24’s team on the ground reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Philippine couple married in hip-deep floodwaters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abe4f0b45892ba3b98c771f073739a76b43172adab6d8989ea87fbc2f2b8a92b</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-philippine-couple-married-in-hip-deep-floodwaters--6777e4d8da7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-philippine-couple-married-in-hip-deep-floodwaters" /><summary type="html">A Philippine couple tied the knot on Tuesday at a Catholic church swamped in hip-deep waters, as heavy rains had pummelled large parts of the country for a month.</summary></entry><entry><title>FRANCE 24 in Nepal: The unbearable wait for missing relatives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45fb05ca7ab3d5709f771de7a13fb6a4b1adfb21f07641a3737ff50df09007f9</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:03:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-france-24-in-nepal-the-unbearable-wait-for-missing-relatives--a2e8192bd78d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-france-24-in-nepal-the-unbearable-wait-for-missing-relatives" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, the hope of finding survivors is fading daily. Bodies are piling up in morgues, and storage capacity is reaching its limit. For the relatives of the missing, the wait is unbearable. They go from one hospital to another, consult the lists of survivors and scrutinise the photos of unidentified bodies. FRANCE 24's special correspondents met with several of these families at the morgue of Kathmandu University Hospital.</summary></entry><entry><title>FRANCE 24 in Nepal: In Bharatpur, authorities begin burying unidentified bodies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18f073206b6668c03746506fa51620a7a25015f2691d134bd19ec5f773d579f0</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T10:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-france-24-in-nepal-in-bharatpur-authorities-begin-burying-unidentified-bodies--b569fe6efd23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-france-24-in-nepal-in-bharatpur-authorities-begin-burying-unidentified-bodies" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, the death toll continues to rise. Every day, new bodies are recovered, but many remain unidentifiable. Several days after the devastating floods, some are already in an advanced state of decomposition. Faced with the influx of remains, authorities have begun burying them without formal identification, primarily to limit health risks and the strong odours. FRANCE 24's special correspondents traveled to Bharatpur, in southern Nepal, to one of these burial sites.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal tunnel rescuers hit dead ends as search for trapped workers continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec9ee778dfc852b97fcbf7c5b1f6b2dfb61c4a2c9add40c774c722f989eff09c</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:15:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-nepal-tunnel-rescuers-hit-dead-ends-as-they-search-for-trapped-workers--33b5ee997511.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-nepal-tunnel-rescuers-hit-dead-ends-as-they-search-for-trapped-workers" /><summary type="html">Rescue teams in Nepal were still searching Wednesday for hundreds of workers believed to have been trapped inside sprawling hydropower tunnels since the catastrophic flash flood that swept through the Himalayan region last week. Officials said that many of the tunnels remain totally blocked by mud and debris.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong pleads guilty to foreign collusion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93e37c1bc5f6fee348b27c3e34f7fedcaddfaff247920d423e1da241517152b4</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T03:23:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-to-foreign-collusion--c6ebc723524d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-to-foreign-collusion" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong on Wednesday pleaded guilty to colluding with foreign powers in a trial that could see the 29-year-old spend the rest of his life behind bars. Wong rose to international prominence for his involvement in the 2014 Umbrella Movement and the mass protests against Beijing that rocked the financial hub in 2019.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>USS Lincoln carrier docks near Thailand's Pattaya resort after nine months at sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91609196517d855c7257550deaa84c8833bf6dabf9f22858d3132cac5cba7420</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T02:37:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-uss-abraham-lincoln-aircraft-carrier-docks-in-thailand-after-nine-months-at-sea--c9055b9c7d8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-uss-abraham-lincoln-aircraft-carrier-docks-in-thailand-after-nine-months-at-sea" /><summary type="html">More than 5,000 US sailors and Marines arrived in Thailand Wednesday after nine months at sea on the USS Abraham Lincoln aircraft carrier. The carrier's long deployment in the Middle East during the US-Israeli war on Iran sparked reports of worsening mental health crises on board, including attempted suicides.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Mass burials held in Nepal as bodies wash up after catastrophic flooding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d162359e92b64b3f120265d25774e284333274d4a47e8908b04cd649c0dbec3</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:40:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mass-burials-held-in-nepal-as-bodies-wash-up-after-catastrophic-flooding--58c2aaea3b6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mass-burials-held-in-nepal-as-bodies-wash-up-after-catastrophic-flooding" /><summary type="html">Every day, new bodies are recovered in Nepal, but many remain unidentifiable. Several days after the disaster, some are already in an advanced state of decomposition. Morgues in the country's main cities are reaching capacity. Faced with the influx of remains, authorities have begun burying them without formal identification. France 24's special correspondents traveled to Bharatpur, in southern Nepal, to one of these burial sites.</summary></entry><entry><title>After the floods, Nepal works to bury hundreds of washed-up unidentified bodies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9974c8405d7fc3b7a4d818a3c3d3c7b88e3790ff692480d0fa6d958cc32fcbdb</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:08:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-works-to-bury-hundreds-of-washed-up-unidentified-bodies--bc87514a0be9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-works-to-bury-hundreds-of-washed-up-unidentified-bodies" /><summary type="html">Nepal is burying dozens of bodies in multiple trenches as Nepal’s disaster agency said that 1,003 deaths had been counted there, with 3,916 people missing, including 583 foreign nationals. In its latest update, China reported 16 deaths and 546 missing, including 261 foreigners. Crews faced challenging conditions as they searched unstable terrain and piles of debris. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal's rescuers navigate mud-swamped tunnels for hundreds of missing workers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7dd44a7695793a62bc47c916a036ba8d68e82358850eadddfba427b4581d7fe</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:59:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-s-rescuers-navigate-mud-swamped-tunnels-for-hundreds-of-missing-workers--afd55fd213ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-s-rescuers-navigate-mud-swamped-tunnels-for-hundreds-of-missing-workers" /><summary type="html">The death toll in Nepal has crossed 1,000 from the deadly floods that tore through an area on the border with Tibet on August 26, and nearly 4,000 people remain missing. six days on hopes for survivors are dimming, but rescuers focused on a network of hydropower sites along the Trishuli River are holding out hope. Of the roughly 900 workers missing, some 500 people are believed to be trapped in the tunnels, according to Nepalese authorities.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal races to find hundreds stuck in hydropower tunnels following floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44bb0456188799ae6eca7dae87e02b26f2175fc972a9e72e2e54ee372e1f0637</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:53:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-hundreds-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-following-floods--ef327437c75e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-hundreds-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-following-floods" /><summary type="html">More than 1,000 people have been killed in the devastating floods that struck the border between Nepal and Tibet. Authorities have started mass burials for unclaimed bodies while they wait for victims' families to claim them. Meanwhile, rescue operations are underway to rescue hundreds of workers stuck in hydropower tunnels. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more from the Chitwan district in Nepal.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tibetan activists accuse China of underreporting flood death toll</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c312f246bf7139087767fa961974077ca7a9c19e3b41dbefaf039b748e8514a1</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T07:59:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260901-tibetan-activists-accuse-china-of-underreporting-flood-death-toll--3962fa94e61e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260901-tibetan-activists-accuse-china-of-underreporting-flood-death-toll" /><summary type="html">Tibetan exiles and activists have accused China of severely underreporting the death toll from the devastating Himalayan floods along its border with Nepal. Beijing has reported 16 deaths and 546 missing in Tibet so far and the foreign ministry insists that the release of information has been "open, transparent and timely".</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Glaciers in Himalayas retreating': Nepal floods triggered by 'glacier collapse &amp; massive landslide'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57cb70a2d2c8b9736214d8da318f8f1642a96cc2089da82a36d98c7d59ed99c3</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T06:26:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-glaciers-in-himalayas-retreating-nepal-floods-triggered-by-glacier-collapse-massive-landsli--b54780004ba1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-glaciers-in-himalayas-retreating-nepal-floods-triggered-by-glacier-collapse-massive-landslide" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Joseph Shea, Glaciologist and Associate Professor at the University of Northern BC. Shea argues that the catastrophe should be understood as a compound event in which a glacier failure and a massive landslide occurred together. His analysis places the disaster within the broader, well-established transformation of the Himalayas under climate change. As warming changes high-mountain environments, scientists may increasingly need to identify subtle precursors to rare but potentially devastating cascading hazards.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Sea change: Much of the world's economic GDP has moved to the Asia-Pacific region'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f9a74e979775dc7a1b1bd52474c013e650c4d6dbfea5d9d2d71daa2650720e0</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T05:22:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260901-sea-change-much-of-the-world-s-economic-gdp-has-moved-to-the-asia-pacific-region-rana-mitte--0e4c1b0f2b67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260901-sea-change-much-of-the-world-s-economic-gdp-has-moved-to-the-asia-pacific-region-rana-mitter" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Rana Mitter, historian, author and ST Lee Chair in US-Asia Relations at the Harvard Kennedy School. He discusses the significance of the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) as it pertains to the evolution of a changing international system, this as the bloc holds a summit in Kyrgyzstan's capital Bishkek.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Melting Himalayas? Nepal disaster exposes growing risk of glacial flooding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:374034313254e203223f310abc73ba0aad9dadc56ac21ddd22e73d79216dd04e</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T23:35:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260831-melting-himalayas-nepal-disaster-exposes-growing-risk-of-glacial-flooding--06953269a81c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260831-melting-himalayas-nepal-disaster-exposes-growing-risk-of-glacial-flooding" /><summary type="html">It may well be one of the tragic consequences of global warming. Scientists will tell us whether receding glaciers are to blame for last Wednesday’s ice shelf collapse that triggered a catastrophic flood, cascading down more than 3,000 metres from the Chinese border into Nepal.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal-Tibet flood death toll surpasses 1,000</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61feaf27a24c9285bdbd01688b6488a3d7e3bbc9ef74e97784025227a9b6318d</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T23:34:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-glacial-flood-death-toll-surpasses-900-in-nepal-and-tibet--b52676f3d5eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-glacial-flood-death-toll-surpasses-900-in-nepal-and-tibet" /><summary type="html">Rescuers battled mud and debris Monday as the death toll from devastating glacial floods along the China-Nepal border topped 1,000, with nearly 4,500 people still missing. Rescue teams continued a desperate search for survivors as entire communities were swept away.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal disaster: Fake and AI images flood social media as deaths mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae5597333332ace73e0da8966c8163f4d2ae45c31cd438eeff4c058299712168</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T20:00:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-disaster-fake-and-ai-images-flood-social-media-as-deaths-mount--1d940b31fc6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-disaster-fake-and-ai-images-flood-social-media-as-deaths-mount" /><summary type="html">As deadly floods hit the Nepal-China border, social media is being inundated with fake and misleading footage. In Truth or Fake, Vedika Bahl goes through viral videos falsely linked to the disaster, including AI-generated content and old recycled footage from India, Chile and Alaska. Some posts have racked up millions of views online, exploiting the tragedy to drive engagement for easy clicks or further perpetuate conspiracy theories.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds feared stuck in hydropower tunnels as flood deaths surpass 950 in Nepal and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b9e4f2619e89165326abef1a477ffe44b0e0a442c42f290ac26374955574821</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T18:34:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/hundreds-feared-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-as-flood-deaths-surpass-950-in-nepal-and-china--666c35c75ae1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hundreds-feared-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-as-flood-deaths-surpass-950-in-nepal-and-china" /><summary type="html">Rescuers raced Monday to free hundreds of workers believed to be trapped in tunnels at hydropower sites that were buried in mud by catastrophic flooding on the Nepal-China border, as the death toll climbed and increasingly desperate families searched for missing loved ones. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal floods 'unprecedented', requires new 'engineering approaches, risk-sensitive urban planning'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:199bceafabf5447d6a16a2d7f513622ac689ac55a498973017d08871e204c751</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:52:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning--f18b77019ec7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning" /><summary type="html">Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Dr. Basanta Raj Adhikari, Director of the Center for Disaster Studies at Tribhuvan University’s Institute of Engineering.  He describes the disaster as an illustration of the limits of conventional prevention in the Himalayas. With flood velocities estimated at 170 to 180 kilometres per hour and hazards ranging from ice and snow avalanches to glacial lake outburst floods, he argues that comprehensive monitoring of Nepal’s exceptionally steep and complex mountain terrain is effectively impossible. Yet Adhikari’s analysis is not fatalistic. Instead, he shifts the emphasis from attempting to predict every extreme event toward risk-informed adaptation. Nepal, he argues, should identify high-risk hotspots through satellite observation, supplement these with ground-based monitoring and early-warning systems, and incorporate that knowledge into risk-sensitive land-use planning.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canberra's zoo treats its residents to personnalised musical therapy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f18283a1091b5c18fa41cb6e85d5cae9dc4471ed743a3171951bcafd9b700b6</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:30:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy--0d0087f76a83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/canberra-s-zoo-treats-its-residents-to-personnalised-musical-therapy" /><summary type="html">A music therapist in Australia has been playing for animals at Canberra's zoo for the last five years. It's a relaxing experience for animals and staff alike and the animals all react differently to the music played.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal deadly floods: FRANCE 24 report – on the ground with survivors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fba8692eb532318b3cae5974cb439838387a457e1170f094020dee1aedad504</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:12:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-_-on-the-ground-with-survivors--b891d1208ba1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-nepal-deadly-floods-france-24-report-%E2%80%93-on-the-ground-with-survivors" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. While rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur in the Nuwako district – one of the villages hit by the flood on August 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal grapples with destruction and loss in wake of deadly floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80d7d21c7555f693b10c75c39eaba9cddbc9c162d19bc3319641a8e5261942e1</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:10:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods--17641910cea0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-grapples-with-destruction-and-loss-in-wake-of-deadly-floods" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Nepal have warned of possible fresh flooding after water levels rose in the Bhotekoshi River. The floods took place after a glacier collapse. They have killed at least 900 people - with more than 4,000 others missing in Nepal and Tibet. Now, a massive rescue effort continues and communities grapple with devastation and loss.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal races to find its missing as flood area remains largely inaccessible</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:340dc44fed67beb7bd85eb11a4005cb17e9ec1a1d6d0d04b435a760c3075f4b7</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:41:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible--450be663b9f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-its-missing-as-flood-area-remains-largely-inaccessible" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rescuers are racing against the clock to find the over 4,000 people missing after the flash floods that devastated an area in the north of the country on August 26. Rescue operations include one where workers are trying to save hundreds believed to be stuck inside a blocked hydropower project. Meanwhile, authorities have started burying unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>After the floods, Nepal's survivors look to rebuilding their lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2f9055c1a88f99f0c484e56cf2f063cde8beb4a7e02f54f8949ad371f271a3f</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:53:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives--e039613e514e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-the-floods-nepal-s-survivors-look-to-rebuilding-their-lives" /><summary type="html">In Nepal, after the deadly flood, another ordeal begins for the survivors: finding shelter, food, and simply the means to survive. In the devastated villages, families lost everything in minutes. And while rescue workers continue searching for possible survivors, those who escaped the disaster are trying to rebuild their lives, despite the threat of another flood. FRANCE 24's special correspondents visited Sinchaur, in the Nuwako district, one of the villages hit by the flood of August 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal starts burying its dead as search for over 4,200 missing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:225bba5f94e8004a7d2864c7b9c9d2f0a868e6fedec57f9723455da8dafaaea2</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:33:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nepal-starts-burying-its-dead-as-search-for-over-4-200-missing-continues--d8984474f7d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-starts-burying-its-dead-as-search-for-over-4-200-missing-continues" /><summary type="html">The combined deaths in Nepal and China surpassed 900, with more than 4,700 people missing. It also includes 933 workers on hydropower projects along the river which the torrent crashed through. With morgues running at full capacity, the country has started to bury unclaimed bodies. FRANCE 244s Shazaib Wahlah tells us more from a grief-stricken Nepal.</summary></entry><entry><title>What to know about the SCO, the summit billed as a counterweight to US influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2e5690809bc9df4498034c525292945d9f553b9c26afbcfcaa4ed7883f1e941</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:31:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-sco-the-summit-billed-as-a-counterweight-to-us-influence--bcde7c336260.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-sco-the-summit-billed-as-a-counterweight-to-us-influence" /><summary type="html">The leaders of China, Russia and India are among the heads of state gathering in Kyrgyzstan for the summit of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization. The summit is celebrating its 25 years in existence. Although the group is billed as a counterweight to US. global influence, it is not the case for all participating countries. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry takes a look at what the SCO is, and what will be discussed this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal rescue teams seek hundreds of workers trapped in hydropower tunnels by deadly floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aec8fde555d402e5ea0f95166437decdb43add904598935be2bb0b7cecc3bd68</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:15:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-rescue-teams-seek-hundreds-of-workers-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels-by-deadly-floods--361362dcb3af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-rescue-teams-seek-hundreds-of-workers-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels-by-deadly-floods" /><summary type="html">Supported by experts from China and India, Nepal's rescue teams on Monday endeavoured to reach hundreds of workers believed to be trapped in hydropower tunnels blocked by the devastating flood of mud, water and debris that swept through the Himalayan region last week.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>What justice for Nepal after flooding?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76a2d7ca7b6ecd68815586f461bd4b5ab087dac0742766cf19ba3075868bad99</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T07:54:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260831-what-justice-for-nepal--ce44c0b4ecf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260831-what-justice-for-nepal" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, August 31: The international press tell the story of a heroic headmaster in Nepal who managed to save more than 1,600 pupils, while the Nepali press lambast a lack of accountability for major polluters. Meanwhile in France, back-to-school season reopens wounds over child sex abuse in before- and after-school clubs. Finally, do ants and bees have a concept of voting?</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal buries victims of Himalayan flooding as death toll climbs past 900</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59ec3c432fd5a9675e4982e118e2537c011a909a3dad29aa3d83a0446a218dea</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T05:46:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-buries-victims-of-himalayan-flooding-as-death-toll-climbs-past-900--38c4dbe0877d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-nepal-buries-victims-of-himalayan-flooding-as-death-toll-climbs-past-900" /><summary type="html">Nepal on Monday began mass burials for the hundreds of people killed in catastrophic flash floods along the Nepal-Tibet border last week, as authorities announced the death toll had climbed past 900 people. Officials in Nepal and neighbouring China are still searching for more than 4,000 missing people, including hundreds of hydropower plant workers across the remote Himalayan region.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry></feed>
